{
  "comment": "UI kits layer pin. scripts/fetch-uikits.mjs reads this to bake every kit into <cache>/uikits/<kit>/. Baked kits fetch first-party npm tarballs (registry.npmjs.org, sha512 verified) or GitHub repo tarballs (codeload.github.com at the pinned ref, resolved sha recorded in provenance.json); pointer kits cache only the site's first-party llms.txt index (robots-gated, like Base UI) because their licences restrict component redistribution or gate access. Every baked kit's LICENSE file is read from its own archive and its sha256 recorded; a kit whose licence file is missing or does not match the pinned spdx is skipped, recorded as a gap, and its previous bake is removed, so a licence change upstream never leaves stale code served. GitHub refs are full commit shas (source.branch records where each sha came from), so a bake is reproducible from this file alone and the fetcher makes no API call. To bump one: git ls-remote https://github.com/<repo> <branch>, put the sha in ref, and re-run npm run uikits. A URL extra is pinned the same way and carries the sha256 the fetched bytes must match. excludes.files are globs over a file name (* matches within the name): tests, fixtures and binary assets stay out of a docs-and-source layer. Bump a version here and re-run npm run uikits to refresh.",
  "excludes": {
    "dirs": [
      "__tests__",
      "__mocks__",
      "__snapshots__",
      "__fhir_tests__",
      "node_modules",
      ".github",
      "testdata"
    ],
    "files": [
      "*.test.*",
      "*.spec.*",
      "*.snap",
      "*.woff2",
      "*.woff",
      "*.ttf",
      "*.otf",
      "*.eot",
      "*.png",
      "*.gif",
      "*.jpg",
      "*.jpeg",
      "*.webp",
      "*.ico",
      "*.svg",
      "*.pdf",
      "*.mp4",
      "*.webm",
      "*.zip"
    ]
  },
